A||||11||LZeitgeist||OPEL SPEEDSTER HEADED FOR U.S. AS 'FIERO'||||1||
Z||000000||LZeitgeist||04-01-2001||11:56 AM||||In a press release given to Road & Track Magazine, Pontiac reveals that the Opel Speedster has been retooled with a new, more comfortable interior and will be released in the 2002 model year, rebadged as the Pontiac Fiero...<P>"With the mid-engine design, the stylish looks and the performance handling of this automobile, we felt it was truly the proper time to take the Fiero name out of mothballs, so to speak. We purchased the name back from a small moped company it had been sold to a few years ago for an undisclosed sum and have tweaked it slightly to attune it to current market preferences.<P>"For the first time, Pontiac will be offering the new Fiero with a turbocharging option for the GT's and Formulas, and the Formula will come standard with a rear wing spoiler and five-point racing harnesses color-matched to the body finish.<P>"We at Pontiac were stunned and embarassed at the way the original Fiero turned out to be the red-headed bastard stepchild of an otherwise incredible historical lineup, and so by offering this new, upgraded performance car, it is our way of apologizing to the wretched refuse that actually spent their hard-earned dollars on that utterly failed plastic-coated marketing experiment. <P>"Now we can truly bring pride to the Fiero name. By having another automobile company build these cars for us, if it turns out to be another royal floperoo, we can just put the blame on Opel and tell the world that they sold us crap."<P>||||reg||1
